## STEP 9 -- reboot persistence: NOT MEASURED, and why

🔴 **This case did not reload the DUT and did not write to startup-config, so persistence across
a reboot is NOT MEASURED. It is not claimed anywhere in this log.**

The reason is bench-level, not a choice about this case. The L3 underlay that the whole campaign
depends on -- `interface vlan10 10.38.22.34/27` on port1.0.10 and `interface vlan48
10.38.22.66/27` on port1.0.48 -- exists in **running-config only**; the boot config is
`flash:/default.cfg`, which does not contain it. A reload therefore destroys the path to the SNMP
manager, the trap receiver and the sFlow collector that the remaining cases of this group need,
and writing the underlay to startup-config is a change to the standing bench
(STANDING-ORDERS §4), which is never taken unattended.

Group A recorded the identical gap, and it is already in the queue as a NEEDS TEST ENGINEER item.
Nothing new is asked here.

