## Verdict

Every limb of RMON that this platform offers was exercised and measured against a counted
stimulus with a control in the same window: the etherStats group appears in the MIB with the
right data source and owner and counts an exact number of frames; the history group lays down
10-second buckets of which the one containing the burst holds exactly 1000 packets and 86000
octets; an alarm on a real counter crosses a real threshold and produces a real SNMPv2c trap on
the wire carrying the right alarm index, variable, sample type, value and threshold, with its log
twin agreeing to the value; a control alarm built identically stays silent throughout and then
fires with the exact count when its own condition is met; and removal takes it off the CLI, out
of the MIB and off the wire, with the identical stimulus producing nothing.

Two deviations were found and are reported rather than graded around, neither of which touches a
measured claim: the per-frame-size counters count both directions where RFC 2819 says received
only, and an out-of-range threshold is reported as `% Unrecognized command` against a later
keyword while `falling-threshold 0` is unconfigurable at all. Reboot persistence is **NOT
MEASURED** for the bench reason stated under STEP 9.

VERDICT: PASS -- RMON statistics, history, event and alarm all measured against counted traffic, with four real traps on the wire, matched controls and clean removal; two product deviations recorded (size buckets count both directions; out-of-range threshold misreported); reboot persistence NOT MEASURED, no reload is possible in this campaign.
